potential if kept concealed, especially since I already have two concealed pungs (B2\u00d73, B5\u00d73). With careful play, I can aim for 8+ points needed to win.\n\nReason: \nPassing preserves the concealed status of my hand, which is crucial for scoring \"Fully Concealed Hand\" (4 points) and \"Two Concealed Pungs\" (2 points). With B2(\u00d73) and B5(\u00d73) already formed as concealed pungs, and good tile availability in the Dots suit, I have strong potential to complete an \"All Pungs\" hand (6 points) while maintaining concealment. This path offers 8+ points minimum if executed properly, whereas Peng T2 would expose my strategy and limit scoring to basic patterns.\n\nAnswer: Pass"}
