 wait for T9/T5 to form additional sequences\n\nReason: \nPassing maintains the concealed hand bonus and provides better flexibility for high-scoring patterns. Chi T8 would expose my hand early without a clear path to 8+ points. The unshown tile distribution favors waiting for B4 or B7 to complete Dot sequences while keeping the hand concealed, which can score Concealed Hand (2 points), potential All Pungs or Half Flush patterns. The current hand has better winning potential by staying concealed.\n\nAnswer: Pass"}
